WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.630
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:26.900 --> 00:32.450
Mr. Lee, if you had taken a taxi all the way home, you probably wouldn't have made it to work tomorrow.

3
00:32.820 --> 00:39.290
We worked late into the night, and I'm sorry to intrude on your home, Mr. Kang.

4
00:39.290 --> 00:43.790
Intrude? It's better than being alone.

5
00:44.040 --> 00:47.590
Sleep on the couch in the living room. I'll get you a blanket.

6
01:21.460 --> 01:25.039
Why are you looking at me like that? I said go wash up.

7
01:29.210 --> 01:31.260
Mr. Kang...

8
01:32.470 --> 01:33.930
What?

9
01:36.759 --> 01:39.020
Can I really...

10
01:39.520 --> 01:42.890
just sleep on the couch?

11
01:55.660 --> 02:00.200
Ko Taewoon / Kim Dohyun

12
02:12.090 --> 02:16.760
Baek Seunghoon / Lee Kyungwon

13
02:28.270 --> 02:35.700
Twisted Tie

14
02:35.700 --> 02:38.990
Episode 1. The Team Leader's Office Perks

15
03:10.110 --> 03:13.990
- Mr. Lee. - Yes, Mr. Kang.

16
03:15.900 --> 03:20.490
You call this a proposal for the VVIP Ocean View Lounge?

17
03:20.490 --> 03:23.329
Is this traffic flow the best you can do?

18
03:25.200 --> 03:32.750
Does the client have to walk down this narrow hallway staring only at imported marble walls?

19
03:37.760 --> 03:40.760
Is a pretty design everything?

20
03:40.760 --> 03:44.350
You have absolutely no understanding of the space right now.

21
03:45.770 --> 03:47.520
I apologize.

22
03:47.520 --> 03:52.690
I was so focused on the point wall that I missed checking the traffic flow.

23
03:57.820 --> 04:01.780
Spend your time coming up with a revision instead of making excuses.

24
04:01.780 --> 04:05.370
Yes, I will redo it right away.

25
04:10.710 --> 04:15.340
Mr. Kang, he's a rookie. Aren't you being a bit too hard on him?

26
04:15.710 --> 04:18.839
Mr. Lee was tearing up a bit earlier.

27
04:18.839 --> 04:23.970
Do clients pay less because he's a rookie?

28
04:26.810 --> 04:32.360
If you baby him, he'll stay at that level forever.

29
04:35.110 --> 04:38.320
[Weather Agency - Heavy Rain & Thunderstorm Warning] Heavy localized rain and thunderstorms across Seoul around 9 PM tonight.

30
05:06.560 --> 05:10.310
Mr. Lee, don't take it to heart.

31
05:10.310 --> 05:15.520
The whole team knows Mr. Kang is a cold-blooded perfectionist who wouldn't bleed a drop if you pricked him.

32
05:15.520 --> 05:21.740
- Exactly, you're just a rookie. - Honestly, doesn't Mr. Kang seem to have a bit of a sociopath in him?

33
05:21.740 --> 05:28.580
Just because he's perfect, does he think everyone is a robot? You must have felt so unfairly treated, Mr. Lee.

34
05:28.620 --> 05:30.750
No.

35
05:30.750 --> 05:33.540
Actually, everyone.

36
05:33.540 --> 05:37.420
I have to disagree with what you just said.

37
05:37.420 --> 05:42.680
- I was just trying to take your side... - Mr. Kang was exactly right.

38
05:42.680 --> 05:48.560
I got so obsessed with the point wall that I completely ruined the basic client traffic flow.

39
05:48.560 --> 05:52.480
Just because a design is pretty doesn't make it a good space.

40
05:52.480 --> 05:55.480
I made a very amateur mistake.

41
05:55.480 --> 05:59.610
He might not be wrong, but his words are a bit cold...

42
05:59.610 --> 06:03.740
He's not cold, he's rational.

43
06:03.740 --> 06:07.580
When he said that babying someone keeps them at that level,

44
06:08.490 --> 06:13.500
it genuinely hit me like a ton of bricks. I had a huge realization.

45
06:13.500 --> 06:18.670
I don't know how he pinpoints the core issue without a single margin of error...

46
06:19.380 --> 06:20.800
He is truly amazing.

47
06:20.800 --> 06:27.220
- Are you being gaslit by Mr. Kang? - It's a severe case. That's quite a talent.

48
06:27.220 --> 06:31.270
That's right, I need to work my fingers to the bone to meet Mr. Kang's standards.

49
06:31.270 --> 06:36.270
I'm going to completely redo the 3D rendering right now. Keep up the good work.

50
06:40.690 --> 06:42.860
What's up with him?

51
06:42.860 --> 06:48.450
I think a crazy guy just joined our team.

52
07:08.680 --> 07:11.760
Great work today, everyone.

53
07:11.760 --> 07:14.640
Those who went out for afternoon meetings can leave right away,

54
07:14.640 --> 07:18.940
and the rest of you, just finish up what you're doing and head home early.

55
07:18.940 --> 07:22.900
- Yes, great work. - I'll be leaving first.

56
07:22.900 --> 07:25.320
Great work today.

57
07:25.320 --> 07:27.320
What are you doing after this?

58
07:30.370 --> 07:33.370
- Mr. Lee. - Yes?

59
07:34.750 --> 07:38.750
Mr. Lee, make sure you get this approved today before you leave.

60
07:39.080 --> 07:44.260
In order for Mr. Baek to order the imported materials, it needs to be finalized by tomorrow morning.

61
07:44.260 --> 07:47.760
Ah... um, by today?

62
07:50.300 --> 07:55.600
Ah, to run the 3D rendering again, it'll probably take past midnight...

63
07:56.100 --> 07:57.890
Why?

64
07:58.520 --> 08:00.560
Do you have a problem with that?

65
08:01.400 --> 08:05.030
Ah, no. I will definitely finish it by today.

66
08:05.030 --> 08:07.070
Please go ahead and leave first.

67
08:07.860 --> 08:13.030
I'll be staying too. I need to approve it as soon as it's done.

68
09:06.460 --> 09:07.960
Mr. Kang.

69
09:10.380 --> 09:15.600
The rendering for the revision is complete. Could you take a look?

70
09:18.680 --> 09:23.810
It's already midnight. Good job, Sunwoo. Let's see.

71
09:40.710 --> 09:44.830
Wow... It's pouring down hard.

72
09:46.090 --> 09:50.630
Mr. Lee, where did you say you lived?

73
09:53.550 --> 09:57.010
- Was it around Gimpo? - Ah, yes.

74
09:57.010 --> 10:00.890
Ah, but with this much rain at this hour,

75
10:00.890 --> 10:04.100
I'm not sure if I can catch a taxi.

76
10:07.110 --> 10:09.400
Even if you catch one, it's a problem.

77
10:10.030 --> 10:14.740
The Olympic Expressway is probably completely flooded by now.

78
10:16.450 --> 10:20.870
Ah, I should look for a nearby sauna. I have a morning meeting tomorrow, and if I'm late...

79
10:20.870 --> 10:25.540
If you go to a sauna, how are you going to come to work smelling like sweat tomorrow?

80
10:30.420 --> 10:40.510
I refuse to see my team member face a client in a wrinkled shirt, reeking of sweat.

81
10:46.850 --> 10:50.020
Pack your bag. We're going to my place.

82
10:50.020 --> 10:54.240
Ah... Ah, no. How could I go to your place, Mr. Kang... I'll figure it out...

83
10:54.240 --> 10:59.370
Mr. Lee. I hate repeating myself.

84
11:00.330 --> 11:05.830
My place is 5 minutes from here, so just follow me without another word.

85
11:43.450 --> 11:47.370
Why are you looking at me like that? I said go wash up.

86
11:52.380 --> 11:53.840
What?

87
11:56.420 --> 12:01.600
Can I really just sleep on the couch?

88
12:17.950 --> 12:23.620
- You're crossing the line, Mr. Lee. - Mr. Kang.

89
12:28.250 --> 12:34.170
Stop talking nonsense and just go in and wash up. You'll catch a cold.

90
12:34.170 --> 12:38.720
Ah, I'm- I'm sorry. Ah, I must have been crazy for a second.

91
12:39.760 --> 12:42.300
The towels are in the cabinet.

92
12:44.050 --> 12:46.770
Yes, thank you.

93
13:29.230 --> 13:31.770
Mr. Kang's scent...

94
13:38.360 --> 13:41.700
Ah, I must be crazy. Seriously, what's wrong with me?

95
14:00.970 --> 14:06.100
Lee Sunwoo, this is Mr. Kang Dojin's house.

96
14:06.100 --> 14:08.760
He's your team leader.

97
14:14.440 --> 14:18.190
Just quietly breathe and sleep.

98
14:18.190 --> 14:25.030
Just sleep on the couch, quietly breathing. Yeah, I can do this.

99
14:54.390 --> 14:58.610
The clothes look really tight on you. That must be uncomfortable.

100
14:58.610 --> 15:03.030
Ah, no. The... scent is nice too,

101
15:03.030 --> 15:05.610
and it's extremely comfortable... Yes.

102
15:12.040 --> 15:15.210
Don't just stand there, come and sit down.

103
15:35.480 --> 15:37.140
Mr. Kang,

104
15:37.140 --> 15:42.570
you give off a very different vibe like this.

105
15:46.490 --> 15:50.160
If I acted like Team Leader Kang Dojin outside of work,

106
15:50.160 --> 15:53.240
how could anyone live without suffocating?

107
15:58.580 --> 16:01.460
You worked hard today, Sunwoo.

108
16:01.460 --> 16:03.250
What?

109
16:17.730 --> 16:22.230
You must have been frantic with me pushing you so hard, right?

110
16:24.820 --> 16:30.700
Still, I think it's admirable that you didn't run away and saw it through to the end.

111
16:59.810 --> 17:02.310
But Sunwoo,

112
17:03.440 --> 17:06.730
what have you been staring at since earlier?

113
17:10.359 --> 17:13.950
If you stay completely frozen like that outside of work too,

114
17:16.369 --> 17:18.750
it's no fun for me.

115
17:46.650 --> 17:49.110
Ah... Ah.

116
17:49.110 --> 17:51.990
M... Mr. Kang. I'm... I'm, I'm sorry.

117
17:51.990 --> 17:54.780
Ah, what did I... just do...

118
17:54.780 --> 17:58.580
I'm sorry... I must have lost my mind, seriously ah...

119
18:05.920 --> 18:07.920
There's no need to apologize.

120
18:10.380 --> 18:12.050
Because it wasn't bad.

121
18:17.810 --> 18:20.020
It's raining heavily,

122
18:20.930 --> 18:24.100
so go to sleep now. Get a good rest,

123
18:24.980 --> 18:26.810
and I'll see you tomorrow.

124
18:51.050 --> 18:56.510
If you act like this, seriously, how am I supposed to hold back...

125
19:04.730 --> 19:09.400
Yes, this is the design blueprint for our VVIP Ocean View Lounge, focusing on efficiency and convenience.

126
19:09.400 --> 19:13.030
Yes, that concludes my presentation. Thank you.

127
19:23.950 --> 19:25.370
Mr. Lee.

128
19:27.790 --> 19:31.090
- Are you kidding me? - Pardon?

129
19:31.800 --> 19:36.010
Ah... no. Um... I completely revised it as you pointed out, Mr. Kang...

130
19:36.010 --> 19:38.390
And you call this a revision?

131
19:40.100 --> 19:45.560
I told you to remove the point wall, and you turned the space into a warehouse.

132
19:47.190 --> 19:54.110
I'm sure I told you clearly that just because a design is pretty doesn't make it a good space.

133
19:54.820 --> 19:59.910
- You're lacking the basics, the basics! - Mr. Kang, but I stayed up all night...

134
19:59.910 --> 20:01.530
Haa...

135
20:01.530 --> 20:03.120
What?

136
20:03.580 --> 20:07.120
Is your brain not working because you're tired from staying up all night?

137
20:10.330 --> 20:13.840
Standing in front of a client with this kind of result

138
20:13.840 --> 20:19.260
is not just a matter of your own pride, it's an insult to our entire team.

139
20:20.640 --> 20:22.930
Do it again.

140
20:23.810 --> 20:30.150
If it's still at this level by tomorrow, you are off this project, Mr. Lee.

141
20:35.610 --> 20:38.280
I will keep that in mind.

142
20:43.330 --> 20:46.540
Where are you going? The meeting isn't over yet.

143
20:46.540 --> 20:49.290
I'm going to step out to the restroom for a moment.

144
20:49.290 --> 20:53.340
I think I need to splash some cold water on my face and get my head working.

145
20:53.920 --> 20:55.840
I apologize.

146
20:58.130 --> 21:02.930
Mr. Kang... I've been working so much overtime lately, I guess I'm out of my mind.

147
21:03.890 --> 21:06.310
You were never in your right mind.

148
21:07.770 --> 21:11.140
We'll resume in 10 minutes, so everyone take a break.

149
21:26.830 --> 21:32.000
Team Leader Kang Dojin... Just how far will you push someone to the bottom...

150
21:46.850 --> 21:51.730
So, is your brain working now that you've splashed some cold water on it?

151
21:52.270 --> 21:58.730
Mr. Kang, no matter how terrible my proposal was, doing that in front of the entire team...

152
21:59.900 --> 22:02.950
Since I trampled on you like that,

153
22:02.950 --> 22:06.030
you're finally glaring at me like a wild beast.

154
22:08.410 --> 22:12.750
Rather than pretending to be a clumsily polite subordinate...

155
22:14.040 --> 22:20.210
it's much better when you act so wronged that you look ready to bite.

156
22:26.970 --> 22:28.970
Are you mad?

157
22:31.810 --> 22:34.810
You started this, Mr. Kang.

158
22:48.700 --> 22:55.120
Mmm hmmm... Mmhmm... Mmm...

159
23:36.250 --> 23:42.420
Twisted Tie
